keys:

    ctrl+t (or ctrl+n)      new shell tab
    ctrl+w                  close tab
    ctrl+→/← (or ctrl+f/b)  next / previous tab


install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash


update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash


make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`.
to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.


Pi status (requires Pi 0.80.4+):

installing or updating tabs installs `~/.pi/agent/extensions/tmux-tabs.js`,
respecting `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. Restart Pi or run `/reload` to load it.
Interactive Pi runs show a blinking dot while working and turn green once
settled, including retries and queued follow-ups. Status clears on session exit.
Print/JSON/RPC runs are ignored. Mid-run permission and question dialogs are
not detected.


development:

    install ShellCheck and shfmt (macOS: brew install shellcheck shfmt).
    on Linux, use your package manager or the upstream release binaries:
      https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck
      https://github.com/mvdan/sh

    make help  list available targets; also the default target
    make fmt   format Bash files in place (4-space indentation)
    make lint  ShellCheck, Bash syntax and read-only formatting checks

    override tool paths with SHELLCHECK=... and SHFMT=... if needed.
